.md
# Real-time ray tracing in a region

This notebook simulates rays moving through a two-dimensional region with circular obstacles. Each particle stores its distance from the boundary, current position, direction, and collision count. The simulation advances in small time steps; near a wall, `RegionNearest` estimates the local boundary normal used to reflect the ray.

The original simulation was adapted from [Tim Laska’s answer to “Why is raytracing so slow?”](https://mathematica.stackexchange.com/questions/219629/why-is-raytracing-so-slow) on Mathematica Stack Exchange. His version precomputes the particle histories and animation frames. This WLJS adaptation advances the state during `Animate` and renders the changing positions and collision-based colors through `GraphicsComplex` allowing to update the vertex data efficiently.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
# Real-time ray tracing in a region

This notebook simulates rays moving through a two-dimensional region with circular obstacles. Each particle stores its distance from the boundary, current position, direction, and collision count. The simulation advances in small time steps; near a wall, `RegionNearest` estimates the local boundary normal used to reflect the ray.

The original simulation was adapted from [Tim Laska’s answer to “Why is raytracing so slow?”](https://mathematica.stackexchange.com/questions/219629/why-is-raytracing-so-slow) on Mathematica Stack Exchange. His version precomputes the particle histories and animation frames. This WLJS adaptation advances the state during `Animate` and renders the changing positions and collision-based colors through `GraphicsComplex` allowing to update the vertex data efficiently.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  InitGroup: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
(* Create and Discretize Region *)
disks = RegionUnion[Disk[{-1, 0}, 0.5], Disk[{1, 0}, 0.5], 
   Disk[{0, -1}, 0.5], Disk[{0, 1}, 0.5], Disk[{0, 0}, 0.25]];
region = RegionDifference[Disk[], disks];
R2 = RegionBoundary@DiscretizeRegion[region, AccuracyGoal -> 5];
(* Set up Region Operators *)
rdf = RegionDistance[R2];
rnf = RegionNearest[R2];
(* Time Increment *)
dt = 3 0.001;
(* Collision Margin *)
margin = 1.02 dt;
(* Starting Point for Emission *)
sp = 0.85 Normalize[{1, 1}];
(* Conditional Particle Advancer *)
advance[r_, x_, v_, c_] := 
 Block[{xnew = x + dt v}, {rdf[xnew], xnew, v, c}] /; r > margin
advance[r_, x_, v_, c_] := 
 Block[{xnew = x , vnew = v, normal = Normalize[x - rnf[x]]},
   vnew = Normalize[v - 2 v.normal normal];
   xnew += dt vnew;
   {rdf[xnew], xnew, vnew, c + 1}] /; r <= margin
   
(* Setup simulation *)
nparticles = 500;
ntimesteps = 1200;

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
## Real-time animation

The particle state is kept locally inside `Module`. Each animation frame advances the simulation by the required number of steps before drawing the new positions; returning to the beginning resets the particles

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
## Real-time animation

The particle state is kept locally inside `Module`. Each animation frame advances the simulation by the required number of steps before drawing the new positions; returning to the beginning resets the particles

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Module[{s, rplot = RegionPlot[R2], lasti = Infinity},
  Animate[
    If[lasti > i, 
      lasti = 1; (* reset inner state *)
      s = Table[{rdf[sp], sp, AngleVector[2 Pi RandomReal[]], 0}, nparticles]
    ];
    
    Do[s = (advance @@ # &) /@ s, {i-lasti}];
    lasti = i;
    
    Show[rplot, Graphics[{PointSize[.01],
      GraphicsComplex[s[[All, 2]], Point[Range[nparticles]],
        VertexColors -> (ColorData["Rainbow", (# - 1)/10] & /@ s[[All, 4]])]}]],
    {i, 1, 300, 1}, RefreshRate -> 60]
]

